' diagram-type: sequence
@startuml
title v0006-web-ui - team-owned environment and secret writes without auth

actor "Operator" as operator_actor
participant "Web UI / Browser" as web_browser
participant "API Gateway" as api_gateway
participant "State Registry" as state_registry
database "PostgreSQL" as state_database

operator_actor -> web_browser : submit environment or secret value\n(no selected team or asserted operator)
activate web_browser
web_browser -> api_gateway : operator write\n(no internal identity headers)
activate api_gateway
api_gateway -> api_gateway : strip forged X-FlowAI-* context\nvalidate required operator_id and team_id\nvalidate optional team_name when supplied\ngenerate request_id

alt required context invalid\nor supplied team_name empty/invalid
  api_gateway --> web_browser : reject before write
else target is /admin/*
  api_gateway --> web_browser : reject before State Registry call
else valid allowlisted operator write
  api_gateway -> state_registry : write with configured Operator-ID, Team-ID,\noptional Team-Name only when present, Request-ID
  activate state_registry
  state_registry -> state_registry : authorize parent resources by team_id\nvalidate same-team ownership\nprepare plaintext-free audit metadata
  state_registry -> state_database : atomically persist environment/secret state\nand audit entry
  activate state_database
  state_database --> state_registry : committed identifiers
  deactivate state_database
  state_registry --> api_gateway : canonical identifiers or ownership denial
  deactivate state_registry
  api_gateway --> web_browser : status, headers, body unchanged
end
deactivate api_gateway
web_browser --> operator_actor : render result without exposing secret plaintext
deactivate web_browser

note over state_registry, state_database
  State Registry owns persistence and authorization.
  API Gateway never stores canonical state or secret values.
end note

@enduml
